{"duration": 46.361, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "A surgeon soaked clean towels in harsh acid to save a boy.", "start": 0.05, "end": 2.802}, {"beat": 0, "text": "Surgery in 1865 was a deadly gamble for every patient.", "start": 2.882, "end": 6.189}, {"beat": 1, "text": "At one hospital, sixteen out of thirty-five patients died.", "start": 6.389, "end": 9.246}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Open wounds filled with pus, forcing doctors to cut off limbs.", "start": 9.326, "end": 12.333}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Then an eleven-year-old boy arrived with a broken leg.", "start": 12.413, "end": 14.973}, {"beat": 1, "text": "His bone pierced the skin, which usually led to death.", "start": 15.053, "end": 17.563}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Joseph Lister set the bone and used carbolic acid on the leg.", "start": 17.763, "end": 20.729}, {"beat": 2, "text": "He wrapped the wound in tin foil for four days.", "start": 20.809, "end": 22.855}, {"beat": 2, "text": "When Lister checked the skin, he saw no infection.", "start": 22.935, "end": 25.207}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see, it was like cleaning smelly sewage with strong chemicals.", "start": 25.407, "end": 28.291}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Louis Pasteur showed that tiny invisible germs cause decay in open wounds.", "start": 28.491, "end": 32.148}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Lister realized that destroying these micro-organisms would stop infections.", "start": 32.228, "end": 35.62}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Carbolic acid wiped out the germs inside open cuts.", "start": 35.7, "end": 38.546}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Deaths dropped from sixteen in thirty-five down to six in forty.", "start": 38.746, "end": 41.69}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Burned skin from the acid later forced doctors to create germ-free surgery.", "start": 41.77, "end": 45.461}], "words": [{"w": "A", "start": 0.119, "end": 0.144, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "surgeon", "start": 0.194, "end": 0.394, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "soaked", "start": 0.444, "end": 0.594, "line